        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Canals and Waterways: Hampshire and Hampden Canal, Tennessee–Tombigbee Waterway, Farmington Canal\n- Places: Massachusetts, Connecticut, New Haven, Northampton, Connecticut River, Tennessee River, Black Warrior-Tombigbee River system, Demopolis, Alabama\n\nFacts:\n- The Hampshire and Hampden Canal was the Massachusetts segment of the Farmington Canal.\n- The Hampshire and Hampden Canal was the Massachusetts segment of an 86-mile canal that once connected New Haven, Connecticut, to the Connecticut River north of Northampton, Massachusetts.\n- The Tennessee–Tombigbee Waterway, also called the Tenn-Tom, is a 234-mile man-made waterway in the United States.\n- The Tennessee–Tombigbee Waterway extends from the Tennessee River to the junction of the Black Warrior-Tombigbee River system near Demopolis, Alabama.",
